# The processes (roadmap os-server.md P6): init, process 1, starts
# tests/posix/proc.c from /z (TEST_POSIX_PROC), which forks, execs, spawns
# and waits, takes a child's fault and a kill as their signals, uses the
# heap, and is refused a fork once the table is full. The idle program
# waits for a key meanwhile; the test ends when the wait is over. A data
# segment grows by a copy into a new one (ROOT_BRK), so its 6 KB more past
# 33 KB need a second 64 KB block, which DOSBox-X's 1 MB does not have
# free: there the root refuses it, ENOMEM.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_PROC
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 180
---
proc: my parent is init (1): 1
proc: the child: its parent is the forker: yes
proc: a fork (3): exited 3
child: argc 3: /z/child 4 two
child: my pid is the one asked for: yes
child: environ[0] TEST=proc
proc: a fork and an exec (3): exited 3
child: argc 1: /z/child
child: environ[0] (none)
proc: the spawned (1): exited 1
proc: posix_spawn (0): 0
proc: an exec of no file (-1, ENOENT 2): -1, 2
proc: after it (4): exited 4
rx286: proc[7] fault #UD at 0007:{z:proc.rx_ud2}
proc: a child's #UD (SIGILL 4): ended by signal 4
proc: kill (0): 0
proc: the killed (SIGTERM 15): ended by signal 15
proc: kill init (-1, EPERM 1): -1, 1
proc: kill no one (-1, ESRCH 3): -1, 3
proc: 3000 bytes of heap: yes; the break moved: yes
proc: a fork bomb: 13 children, then EAGAIN (11): 11
proc: all 13 reaped; then ECHILD (10): 10
proc: nice to 19 (-1, errno 5 kept): -1, 5
proc: kill(zombie, 0), its session (0 1): 0 1
proc: waitpid with an option it does not know (-1, EINVAL 22): -1, 22
proc: SIGCHLD ignored: no zombie, ECHILD (-1, 10): -1, 10
proc: poll of a terminal without keys, a read's 0 at once (1 POLLIN): 1 1
proc: SIGCONT blocked: pending, then none (1 0): 1 0
proc: a sleep past 2^32 ticks, then an alarm (-1, EINTR 4, 1): -1, 4, 1
@bochs proc: 28 KB and 6 KB more (yes yes), then 32 KB more (no): yes yes no
@bochs proc: and they whole: yes
@mame proc: 28 KB and 6 KB more (yes yes), then 32 KB more (no): yes yes no
@mame proc: and they whole: yes
@dosbox-x proc: 28 KB and 6 KB more (yes yes), then 32 KB more (no): yes no no
proc: done
